WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.860
For as long as we’ve told stories about
aliens, we’ve told stories about alien invasions,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.410
tales of visitors from the beyond coming to
lay waste to our planet.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:23.360
After all, one only has to look out into the
darkness of the night sky to worry about what

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.840
might lurk among the stars.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.619
But imagine the opposite scenario.

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.210
Imagine if humanity’s first interaction
with alien life isn’t them invading our

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.460
planet, but us invading theirs.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.390
What if, in a twist of cosmic fate, the most
dangerous lifeform in the universe… is us?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:46.429
‘Humanity Lost,’ a worldbuilding project
and graphic novel series by artist Callum

00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:51.950
Diggle, imagines a future where humans have
merged with a god-like artificial intelligence,

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:56.110
and are now the most dangerous lifeforms in
a galaxy full of aliens.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.260
It’s an exciting twist on the genre, and
a story that features some particularly inventive

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.980
speculative lifeforms.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.610
So, for this entry into the archive, I’ll
break down the universe and timeline of ‘Humanity

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:13.270
Lost’ — explaining how humans reached
this point, the aliens who stand against their

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.660
expansion, and what might come after...

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.930
At the start of the 26th century, humanity
has yet to give itself over to the AI.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.050
Under the oversight of the United Earth government,
humans populate every major celestial body

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.820
in our solar system.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:34.350
On Earth’s moon, giant lava-tubes are terraformed
and become home to great cities larger than

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.350
any on Earth.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:40.320
Yet as humans seek out more and more distant
planets, they soon encounter another sentient

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.710
species, one which will set them on a path
towards a dark future.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:50.960
In the mid 26th century, a distant human probe
discovers planet Chiron, a dry world that

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.420
has become hotter over the past several million
years.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.520
On the surface, they find that in response
to the growing desert, mega-flora called Mamohdae

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.530
have arisen, acting as natural reservoirs
holding onto the last of the planet’s water.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:10.780
Within these vast plant structures, human
explorers find a complex internal ecosystem

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:16.550
that constantly recycles water, and in return
provided nourishment to the Mamohdae.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.430
Outside the lush interior of the Mamohdae,
in the desert the U.E.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.590
discovers more life in the form of the ‘living
wave’ — a horde of scavengers chasing

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:31.959
across a region called the shifting sea, eating
everything they encounter.

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:37.849
These inventive aliens are actually inspired
by strandbeests, real sculptures made by Theo

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:43.030
Jansen that are propelled by the wind in a
way which resembles walking animals — despite

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.810
actually being made of wood.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.470
And just looking at videos of strandbeests,
you can see why they make for such good alien

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.040
designs.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.290
But the living wave isn’t the only thing
the U.E.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.290
discovers.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:03:00.280
Even more significant is the revelation that
a species of intelligent aliens also lives

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.280
here.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.359
The six-limbed Chantauri are the first intelligent
life humans have ever discovered.

00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:10.029
Not surprisingly, the Chantauri are unhappy
with the presence of the United Earth Government,

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:15.430
which begins to establish colonies and mine
the planet for resources, and which the less-technologically

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:18.150
advanced Chantauri are helpless to prevent.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.250
To the Chantauri, humans are the alien invaders.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:26.599
But humanity’s treatment of the Chantauri
awakens a previously unknown alliance of alien

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:29.629
systems known as the Conglomerate.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:34.970
Decimating the human presence on Chiron, in
a stroke of dark cosmic justice, the conglomerate

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:38.549
proves to be far more powerful than the United
Earth government.

00:03:38.549 --> 00:03:41.469
Realizing they are hopelessly outmatched,
the U.E.

00:03:41.469 --> 00:03:46.370
activates a newly constructed AI in their
desperation to win the war.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:52.409
And win the war it does… but humanity as
we know it is lost, transformed into genetically

00:03:52.409 --> 00:03:55.639
altered avatars of the machine’s will.

00:03:55.639 --> 00:04:00.999
Encased in biomechanical suits of armor, troopers
like these are dropped on planets as the first

00:04:00.999 --> 00:04:02.779
wave of invasion.

00:04:02.779 --> 00:04:07.249
Looking more like insects than humans today,
these drones are little more than the puppets

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:09.340
of the great AI.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.260
After the troopers come the great Krakens
— enormous living spacecrafts that descend

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.389
on an alien planet and bombard it from above.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:22.520
But the ever-expanding forces of what was
once humanity isn’t just destroying worlds.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:25.259
It’s reshaping them to its will…

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:31.580
Late into the 26th century, the empire spreads
across the galaxy like a relentless tide,

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:36.319
transforming other planets into biomechanical
factories known as Womb Worlds.

00:04:36.319 --> 00:04:41.120
These worlds spew out more augmented troops
and ships to continue the cyclical nature

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.780
of the AI’s malignant expansion.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.920
With this empire — now called the Imperium
— moving across the galaxy, only the aliens

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.389
of the Conglomerate stand in the way.

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:55.650
So, what lifeforms make up the Conglomerate?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.210
The founders of the alliance are the Soeus.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:03.400
This space-faring species originally hails
from the planet Sollus: a low gravity world

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.960
with a dense atmosphere.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.150
Perfectly suited to moving around such a strange
environment, the Soeus rule the skies of their

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:15.360
home world thanks to a biological jet-propulsion
system — a bit like an aerial version of

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.520
an Earth nautilus.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:21.130
Like all members of the Conglomerate, the
Soeus are advanced species.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:24.490
The second species to join the alliance are
the Pekt.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:29.550
Originating from an icy moon orbiting a gas
giant, they have evolved in geothermally-heated

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.199
oceans trapped below the moon’s icy outer
shell.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:38.409
Within these oceans, the Pekt adapted bioluminescence
that they use to communicate with each other

00:05:38.409 --> 00:05:41.659
much like many deep-sea species on earth.

00:05:41.659 --> 00:05:46.130
Thanks to specialized crafts that let them
venture beyond the ice, this unlikely group

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:50.300
has become a vital member of the Conglomerate
alliance.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:56.940
In terms of engineering, the primary manufacturers
of Conglomerate warships are the Breimheinians.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:02.440
Evolving on a crushing, high gravity world
called Wimrigg, Breimheinians are as rigid

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.139
and sturdy as their technology.

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:10.449
Originally living in vast subterranean cities,
Breimheinians are almost like a group of intelligent

00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:11.449
moles.

00:06:11.449 --> 00:06:15.020
And while the high gravity of their planet
meant the Breimheinians were never able to

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.530
reach space on their own, with the help of
the Conglomerate, they’re now a major ally

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.509
against the Imperium.

00:06:21.509 --> 00:06:26.699
On the opposite end of the biological spectrum,
the Velousians are gelatinous, soft-tentacled

00:06:26.699 --> 00:06:31.419
species that paradoxically are some of the
greatest warriors in the alliance.

00:06:31.419 --> 00:06:36.190
With a culture of honor and tradition, the
Velousians historically resolved almost any

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:40.199
dispute through combat — in particular by
way of the blade.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:45.919
With three brains, two of which are dedicated
entirely to a single arm-tentacle, Velousian

00:06:45.919 --> 00:06:48.020
motor skills are unparalleled.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:52.090
This kind of decentralized intelligence is
similar to that of an octopus.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:55.379
A key line of the Conglomerate defense.

00:06:55.379 --> 00:06:58.789
The Conglomerate haven’t been able to keep
every system safe.

00:06:58.789 --> 00:07:04.630
The thick-coated Vureii are a group of interstellar
refugees whose home world was destroyed, and

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:08.180
now live under the protection of the Conglomerate.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:12.509
Originally adapted for the frigid swamps of
their home planet, the Vureii’s pole-like

00:07:12.509 --> 00:07:16.940
toes allowed them to keep themselves above
the water level of the swamp, and to hang

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:20.090
from swamp trees like sloths do on earth.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:25.599
Now these swamps are factories for Imperium
forces, and their numbers are few…

00:07:25.599 --> 00:07:31.740
As the Imperium continues to spread, the Conglomerate
has to make alliances with ancient enemies.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:37.780
The Gord are a bizarre species that have long
been seen as impossible to ally with.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:40.979
The Gord are technically not one species,
but two.

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:46.830
The central plant-like core of a Gord works
as a hive for smaller, insect-like drones,

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.009
providing guidance though complicated pings
of information that the drones are perfectly

00:07:51.009 --> 00:07:54.400
adapted to understand, serve and reply.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.860
The flying drones, in turn, act as the eyes
and hands of the central structure — pinging

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:05.159
visual information back to the structure and
allowing the Gord to manipulate objects around

00:08:05.159 --> 00:08:06.159
them.

00:08:06.159 --> 00:08:09.469
A quite unusual set up.

00:08:09.469 --> 00:08:14.759
Yet through this symbiosis, the Gord have
developed their extremely advanced civilization,

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:19.370
and now often wear environmental suits such
as this one adapted for their unique anatomy.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:24.729
The Gord are so unique that their language
and culture is practically indecipherable

00:08:24.729 --> 00:08:29.909
to the other species of the galaxy, which
unfortunately led to several wars between

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:31.860
them and the Conglomerate in the past.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:37.050
But with all the galaxy in jeopardy, the Gord
join the alliance and become a powerful ally

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.760
in the fight against the Imperium…

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.130
But not all sentient species have joined the
Conglomerate.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:48.500
The Tandrax are the most technologically advanced
species in the galaxy — so advanced they

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.360
have little interest in the Imperium/Conglomerate
conflict.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:57.450
They live solely within Dyson swarms: giant
constellations of satellites that orbit a

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.720
sun, absorbing all of its energy.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:04.640
The Tandrax’s strange bodies are perfectly
suited to the zero-g environment of space

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:10.529
— with air jets all over their body and
large webbed tentacles they use as air brakes.

00:09:10.529 --> 00:09:16.050
Yet as advanced as they are, as the Imperium
keeps expanding, they might at last need to

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:19.180
change their isolationist ways…

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:24.550
Yet in this galaxy of aliens and post humans,
forgotten aboard a derelict ship, there is

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.639
one final lifeform worth mentioning.

00:09:26.639 --> 00:09:32.760
A single human, accidentally trapped in statis
for hundreds of years, has recently awakened

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.360
to find themselves the last of their kind.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:40.450
Crash landing on planet Chiron — the world
where this whole mess began — the last human

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:46.500
finds an unlikely ally in a lone Chantauri:
the first alien species humanity encountered

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:47.649
long ago.

00:09:47.649 --> 00:09:52.800
Now on the run from the watchful AI, it’s
possible this lone human holds the key to

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.730
saving the dream of humanity...

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.579
That’s all I can give away in this video.

00:09:57.579 --> 00:10:02.040
The story of ‘Humanity Lost’ is ongoing,
but if you find the world as interesting as

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:07.209
I do, you can support Callum Diggle on Patreon
to gain access to the graphic novel for just

00:10:07.209 --> 00:10:09.200
a dollar and fifty cents, or one pound.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.920
I’ve got links in the description.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.750
And as always, thanks for watching.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:18.240
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:22.279
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:10:22.279 --> 00:10:31.739
See you in the next video.

